.SH NAME
.PP
auto-unsupported-release - Display a user-friendly message for unsupported OS releases

\" Convention:
\" Underline anything that is typed verbatim - commands, etc.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
.nf 
.na
auto-unsupported-release command
.ad
.fi

.SH ARGUMENTS
.nf
.na
command     Name of the calling command, usually $0
.ad
.fi

.SH DESCRIPTION

The
.B auto-unsupported-release
command displays a user-friendly message stating the the
calling script does not support this release of the operating
system running it.
This is used by some auto-admin scripts where a particular
operating system release lacks a necessary feature.

.SH RETURN VALUES

0 on success, non-zero error codes otherwise.

.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
.na
auto-unsupported-release $0
.ad
.fi

.SH SEE ALSO

auto-admin(8), auto-unsupported-os(8), auto-os-release(8)

